WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.040
The "Venom" sequel unleashes a lot of carnage, but&nbsp;
it doesn't have answers for everything you want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.480
know. Will Anne ever dump Dr. Dan and get with a&nbsp;
hero instead of a zero? Will Venom finally meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:14.640
Spider-Man? These are the biggest unanswered&nbsp;
questions in "Venom: Let There Be Carnage."

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.560
In a key scene of the "Venom" sequel, Eddie&nbsp;
Brock goes to visit Cletus Kasady in San Quentin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.800
At first trying to play things cool, Eddie&nbsp;
finally loses it when the convicted serial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.680
killer begins comparing himself to Eddie.&nbsp;
Kasady killed multiple members of his family;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.400
Eddie, he claims, killed a&nbsp;
family member when he was born.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.280
In the comics, Eddie's mother did indeed die&nbsp;
from complications during childbirth — a tragedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:42.400
compounded when his father, Carl Brock, came to&nbsp;
treat the child with an icy, angry detachment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.280
Much of what Eddie became — athlete, star student,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.280
journalist — was in a desperate attempt&nbsp;
to gain his father's approval and warmth.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.720
In actuality, Brock is somewhat in&nbsp;
the neighborhood of Cletus Kasady.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.400
While that first death may not have been&nbsp;
his doing, an older Brock got drunk in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.600
comics once and accidentally struck and killed a&nbsp;
child with his father's car. In that storyline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.680
Eddie wanted to turn himself in and face&nbsp;
the music, but his dad talked him out of it.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:10.400
Whichever Eddie Brock storylines are making their&nbsp;
way to the silver screen, this much is certain:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.440
Eddie has some serious guilt on his shoulders.&nbsp;
Kasady knows exactly which buttons to push,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:19.280
and when Eddie gets mad, Venom wants&nbsp;
to help his buddy out. But ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:24.160
this fit of rage only leads to Kasady taking in&nbsp;
the symbiote, causing more death and destruction.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.360
"Is Venom gay?" Those are three words you most&nbsp;
likely didn't think you'd be asking yourself on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.840
the way out of the theater, but it's a very real&nbsp;
question that the movie definitely brings up.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.160
"Venom: Let There Be Carnage" has a scene where&nbsp;
the symbiote, on the rebound after a bad breakup&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:43.200
with Eddie, finds himself at a San Francisco&nbsp;
rave. After turning down the advances of a woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.040
the alien gets up on stage and delivers&nbsp;
a rant that includes the declaration:

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.960
"I am out of the Eddie closet."

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.600
Speaking about the movie's credited writers,&nbsp;
Kelly Marcel and Tom Hardy, Serkis implied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:58.080
that the scene very much means what you think&nbsp;
it means. He shared in an interview with Uproxx,

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.120
"Tom and Kelly were always about&nbsp;
Venom coming out and going to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.360
party that was a very sort of an&nbsp;
LGBTQIA kind of festival, really,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.080
I'd call it. So, this is his coming out party&nbsp;
basically. This is Venom's coming-out party."

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.280
We already know that Venom has a&nbsp;
certain degree of gender fluidity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.840
The symbiote inhabits genders indiscriminately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.480
and although Venom has come to appreciate Eddie&nbsp;
Brock (even at one point declaring love for him),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:25.520
Venom also seems to enjoy inhabiting old&nbsp;
Mrs. Chen's body and having Anne get flirty.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.360
The bottom line? By the end of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.800
Venom seems happy and comfortable&nbsp;
with himself. That's all that matters.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:31.760
"You bet your ass."

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:37.280
"Venom: Let There Be Carnage" doesn't give viewers&nbsp;
any idea where Shriek, aka Frances Barrison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.640
got her powers. Specifically, we're talking about&nbsp;
her ability to emit an eardrum-piercing scream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:48.480
that can kill humans and temporarily disorient&nbsp;
sound-sensitive symbiotes like Venom and Carnage.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.480
Instead, the audience meets Frances&nbsp;
in a cell at St. Estes Reform School&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.920
adjacent to Cletus Kasady, who&nbsp;
makes her a paper promise ring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.160
before she is whisked off to her new&nbsp;
home at Ravencroft mental institution.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.440
Much of this is because, in a series&nbsp;
where everyone else seems to be gaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.600
powers via symbiotes, Shriek's talents are&nbsp;
derived from her status as what has been a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.320
dirty word for movies based on Marvel&nbsp;
Comics not called "X-Men": "mutant."

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:16.960
Back around the turn of the century, as Marvel&nbsp;
sold rights to various properties to studios,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.440
only 20th Century Fox secured the rights to&nbsp;
the mutant corner of the Marvel universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.800
which it famously used for its&nbsp;
own series of "X-Men" movies.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.440
Now, things appear to be on&nbsp;
the path to mutants finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.760
joining the MCU — but since the "Venom"&nbsp;
films are technically Sony productions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:36.160
in Sony's own Universe of Marvel Characters,&nbsp;
you can see where things get muddled.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.480
In the original Marvel comics, Shriek had a&nbsp;
horrific upbringing that involved physical abuse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.800
body-shaming, drug use, and even being&nbsp;
shot in the head by a police officer.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.760
All this led to the awakening&nbsp;
of her latent mutant abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:53.040
which include sound manipulation, levitation,&nbsp;
and even some psychic powers and mind control.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.840
Based on the explosive end credits&nbsp;
scene of this "Venom" movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.840
it's not likely we'll get answers about&nbsp;
Shriek's mutant origins any time soon.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:04.400
The first time Venom sees Carnage in the&nbsp;
flesh, the black symbiote recedes back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:09.040
into Eddie Brock's body like he's a frightened&nbsp;
Hulk who just saw Thanos walk into the club.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.840
"Oh, shit!"

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:14.753
"Whoa, where are you going?"

00:04:14.753 --> 00:04:15.414
"That is a red one!"

00:04:15.414 --> 00:04:16.485
"You need to come out right now."

00:04:16.485 --> 00:04:16.800
"ROAAAAAR"

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.240
As comic fans know, many symbiote&nbsp;
species have their own colors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:25.200
with Venom being black, Scream colored yellow,&nbsp;
Sleeper being green, and so on. The reason why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.360
Carnage is red is because it entered Cletus&nbsp;
through his bloodstream. In the comics, Eddie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:33.920
was in a prison cell with Cletus when Venom's&nbsp;
spawn accessed Kasady through a cut in his hand.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:38.320
In the movie, a somewhat similar event occurs,&nbsp;
even if it gets tweaked a bit. Although Brock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:42.400
and Kasady aren't in a cell together, the&nbsp;
serial killer manages to bite into Eddie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:46.160
after which he remarks upon the unique&nbsp;
composition of Eddie's inner workings.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.560
"I have tasted blood before, and that is not it."

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.720
Whatever "it" is, it is compounded when&nbsp;
the state tries to put Cletus Kasady to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.720 --> 00:05:00.000
death via lethal injection. Carnage uses&nbsp;
the opportunity to finally seize Kasady,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.200
breaking free from the restraints&nbsp;
and beginning his killing spree.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.560
So, why is Venom so afraid of a&nbsp;
"red one"? Well, for starters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:11.040
anyone can see that Carnage is clearly bigger&nbsp;
and seems to have more weapons at the ready.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:15.680
It's also generally accepted that each spawn of&nbsp;
a symbiote is stronger than the one before it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:18.800
so Venom knows right off the&nbsp;
bat that he's at a disadvantage.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.360
Also, it never helps when the&nbsp;
symbiote you're about to go up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:25.280
against has chosen a host who just so&nbsp;
happens to be a ruthless serial killer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:29.680
But the significance of him being red, and&nbsp;
that being scarier? That's unexplained.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.720
Who knows? Maybe Venom just read&nbsp;
the comic books when he was a kid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.440
and knows with one glance that&nbsp;
he's in for maximum carnage.

